===Russia vs Egypt===
[[File:Rus-Egy (2).jpg|thumb|The Egyptian team lining up]]
The two teams had never met before.<ref name=Kit>{{cite web |url=https://resources.fifa.com/image/upload/2018-fifa-world-cup-russiatm-statistical-kit.pdf?cloudid=fjqkfby8aur1lxnvnxdi |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180508111620/http://resources.fifa.com/image/upload/2018-fifa-world-cup-russiatm-statistical-kit.pdf?cloudid=fjqkfby8aur1lxnvnxdi |url-status=dead |archive-date=8 May 2018 |title=2018 FIFA World Cup – Statistical Kit |website=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association}}</ref>

[[Sergei Ignashevich]] headed at [[Mohamed El Shenawy]] before [[Aleksandr Golovin (footballer)|Aleksandr Golovin]] fired wide. [[Trézéguet (Egyptian footballer)|Trézéguet]] then curled just wide from the edge of the box. Russia took the lead when El Shenawy's clearance punch found [[Roman Zobnin]], whose first-time follow up shot spun in off [[Ahmed Fathy]], with VAR confirming that [[Artem Dzyuba]] had not fouled his opponent.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2018/jun/19/russia-egypt-world-cup-match-report |title=Russia all but qualify for knockout stage with win over Mo Salah's Egypt |date=19 June 2018 |work=Guardian|access-date=20 June 2018}}</ref>

[[Mário Fernandes (footballer)|Mário Fernandes]] soon drove into the box before supplying a cut-back form the right for [[Denis Cheryshev]] to slot home Russia's second with his left foot.<ref>{{cite web |last=Ridge |first=Patric |title=Salah strikes but hosts right on course for last 16 |url=http://www.goal.com/en-sa/match/russia-v-egypt/report/82f9rqwhb5112piklj96v8hd5 |website=Goal.com |date=19 June 2018}}</ref> Dzyuba made it 3–0 as he took a lofted ball into the box down on his chest, taking a touch to go past [[Ali Gabr]] and finish past El Shenawy with a low shot. Salah won a penalty after he was fouled by Zobnin - although it was only given after a consultation with the video assistant referee as the referee had initially said the offence took place outside the area. Salah scored from the spot to become only the third Egyptian player to score at a World Cup.<ref name="BBC Russia v Egypt">{{cite web |last=Emons |first=Michael |title=Russia 3 Egypt 1 |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/44439062 |work=BBC Sport |date=19 June 2018}}</ref><ref name="RUS-EGY recap">{{cite web |url=https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/russia-continue-racing-despite-salah-consolation |title=Russia race on despite Salah consolation |publisher=FIFA |date=19 June 2018 |access-date=19 June 2018 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260520044912/https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/russia-continue-racing-despite-salah-consolation |archive-date=20 May 2026}}</ref>

This is the first time that Russia have won their opening two matches at a World Cup since [[1966 FIFA World Cup|1966]] (as the Soviet Union).<ref name="BBC Russia v Egypt"/> And following with Uruguay's 1–0 victory over Saudi Arabia, Russia, for the first time since the collapse of the Soviet Union, qualified for the next round.

